ComplytEX (SaaS Agent)
User Manual
Version 1.0

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. INTRODUCTION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This document is a functional user manual for the ComplytEX SaaS Agent
application. It explains, module by module, how to use every major page,
form, and tab in the web UI.

The application is a Node.js backend with a static HTML/JavaScript frontend
served from the `public` folder. You typically access it through a browser
(e.g., `http://localhost:3000` or your deployed URL).

Each section below describes:
- Purpose of the page or module
- How to navigate to it
- Explanation of key fields and controls
- Typical user workflows


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. NAVIGATION OVERVIEW
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Main entry points:
- Home / SaaS Agent Dashboard: `/index.html` or `/`
- Login: `/login.html`
- Owner Dashboard: `/dashboard.html`
- Application Shell: `/app.html`

App Shell (`/app.html`) is the recommended way to navigate modules, because it
loads each module inside an iframe and keeps a consistent top header.

In the shell, modules appear on the left as a list:
- Business Setup (Profile)
- Safety Office
- Safety Auditor
- HR & Payroll
- Accounting
- CRM
- Support
- AI

Selecting a module changes the hash in the URL and loads the corresponding
page into the right‑hand iframe.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. AUTHENTICATION MODULE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3.1 Login Page (`/login.html`)

PURPOSE
- Authenticate users into ComplytEX and provide demo logins for typical roles.

HOW TO OPEN
- From the Home page, click "Login"; or navigate directly to `/login.html`.

LAYOUT
- ComplytEX logo at the top.
- Title: "Login".
- Two main input fields and a Sign In button.
- Demo Accounts list with quick login buttons.

FIELDS
- Email
  - Your login email address.
- Password
  - Your password.

ACTIONS
- Sign In
  - Click the **Sign In** button.
  - Sends a POST to `/api/auth/login` with email & password.
  - On success, you are redirected either to a provided redirect URL from the
    server or default `/dashboard`.
  - On failure, an error message appears in the status area.

- Demo Accounts
  - Buttons such as "Login as Owner", "HR Manager", "Sales Manager",
    "Buyer", "Supplier", "Designer", "Safety Auditor", "Safety Office",
    and "Inspection".
  - Clicking a button fills the email and password fields with demo
    credentials and triggers login.

STATUS MESSAGES
- A message box appears after you attempt to sign in:
  - Green background for success ("Signed in!").
  - Red background for errors (e.g., "Login failed" or backend error text).


3.2 Register Page (`/register.html`)

PURPOSE
- Create new tenant or user accounts (implementation may vary by backend).

TYPICAL FLOW (CONCEPTUAL)
- Provide organization/tenant information and admin user credentials.
- Submit the form; on success, you can then log in at the Login page.

(Exact fields depend on your server configuration and are not fully detailed
in the static HTML.)


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. HOME / DEMO DASHBOARD MODULE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4.1 SaaS Agent Dashboard (`/index.html`)

PURPOSE
- Demonstration dashboard to test:
  - Azure SQL Database connectivity.
  - Basic CRUD operations on a demo contacts table (`contactTest`).

HOW TO OPEN
- Default root (`/`) or `/index.html`.

SECTIONS

A. Header Links
- Login → `/login`
- Register → `/register`
- Owner Dashboard → `/dashboard`
- Employees → `/employees`
- Roles → `/roles`
- Support → `/support`
- Billing → `/billing`

B. Database Connection Card
- Button: **Test Database Connection**
- When clicked:
  - Sends POST to `/api/test-connection`.
  - On success, shows:
    - Database name
    - Server name
    - Tables Found (count)
    - Connection Time (timestamp)
  - Stats area also displays table count and server status.

C. Contact Management Card
- Purpose: Add, list, and delete contacts from the demo contacts table.

FIELDS
- Contact Name
  - Single text box for the contact's name.

ACTIONS
- Add Contact
  - Validates that name is non-empty.
  - POST `/api/contacts` with `{ name }`.
  - On success, shows confirmation and updated total contact count.
  - Automatically refreshes the contacts list.

- Refresh List
  - GET `/api/contacts` to reload data.

- Clear All
  - DELETE `/api/contacts` to remove all demo contacts.

D. Contacts List Card

- Displays each contact from `/api/contacts`:
  - Name
  - ID
  - Added date/time

- For each contact:
  - **Edit** button
    - Opens an edit modal.
    - Modal fields:
      - New Name
    - Actions:
      - Save Changes → PUT `/api/contacts/{id}`.
      - Cancel → closes modal.

  - **Delete** button
    - Confirms and then DELETE `/api/contacts/{id}`.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. OWNER DASHBOARD MODULE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

5.1 Owner Dashboard (`/dashboard.html`)

PURPOSE
- Give business owners an overview of their tenant data and key modules.

HOW TO OPEN
- `/dashboard.html` or via link from Home or Login redirects.

FIELDS
- Tenant ID
  - Numeric or identifier for the tenant to load.

- Business Type
  - Manufacturer
  - Buyer
  - Supplier
  - Designer
  - SafetyAuditor
  - SafetyOffice
  - Inspection

ACTIONS
- Load
  - Validates Tenant ID is provided.
  - GET `/api/tenant/{tenantId}/summary`.
  - If successful:
    - Displays tenant name and business type.
    - Fills counts cards:
      - Employees
      - Customers
      - Suppliers
      - Certifications
    - Fills Modules grid based on backend data.
    - Highlights modules most relevant to the selected business type.

SECTIONS
- Summary cards
  - Each card shows a label (Employees, Customers, etc.) and a count.

- Modules grid
  - Grid of modules available to the tenant.
  - Items may be visually emphasized if they are core to the selected
    business type (e.g., HR for Manufacturer, CRM for Buyer, etc.).


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. APPLICATION SHELL MODULE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

6.1 App Shell (`/app.html`)

PURPOSE
- Provide a unified shell with a left navigation pane and a main iframe for
  module content.

LAYOUT
- Top header: ComplytEX logo and title.
- Left card: "Modules" list.
- Right card: iframe titled "Application".

LEFT MODULE LINKS
- Business Setup → hash `#/profile`
- Safety Office → `#/safety`
- Safety Auditor → `#/auditor`
- HR & Payroll → `#/hr`
- Accounting → `#/accounting`
- CRM → `#/crm`
- Support → `#/support`
- AI → `#/ai`

IFRAME URL MAPPING
- `#/profile` → `/profile.html?embedded=1`
- `#/safety` → `/masters/safety-office.html?embedded=1`
- `#/auditor` → `/masters/safety-auditor.html?embedded=1`
- `#/hr` → `/hr/index.html`
- `#/accounting` → `/accounting/dashboard.html?embedded=1`
- `#/crm` → `/crm/index.html`
- `#/support` → `/support.html?embedded=1`
- `#/ai` → `/ai/analyst.html?embedded=1`
- Additional hashes map to other pages (e.g., employees, tracking, report).

RESPONSIVE BEHAVIOR
- The iframe height is dynamically adjusted so the content fits the viewport
  (minus header and footer margins).

TYPICAL USAGE
- Users should log in, navigate to `/app.html`, then switch modules via the
  left list. Each module remains visually consistent due to the shared shell.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. BUSINESS SETUP MODULE (PROFILE)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

7.1 Overview (`/profile.html`)

PURPOSE
- Central configuration area for company profile, warehouses, factory/land,
  spaces, assets, certifications, unions, and an embedded Business Agent.

LAYOUT
- Global header: "BUSINESS SETUP".
- Left panel: Business Setup Tabs (Head Office, Setup, Extended) and
  Business Agent link.
- Center working pane: shows different forms depending on selected tab.
- Right panel: Quick Links (Safety Audits, Training, Attendance Scan,
  AI Analyst).

EMBEDDED MODE
- When opened as `/profile.html?embedded=1`, its own header/sidebars are
  hidden to prevent duplicate headers when inside the shell.


7.2 Company Profile (Head Office) – `companyPane`

HOW TO ACCESS
- From left, choose Company Profile tab (Head Office) or use top tabs.

FIELDS
- Head Office Address 1 (required)
- Address 2
- City
- State / Province
- Postal Code
- Total No. of Employees (required)
- Capacity Type (e.g., units per day)
- Capacity Qty
- Minimum Order Qty
- Sales Profit
  - Type (e.g., percentage or fixed)
  - Value
- Minimum Wage
- Minimum Age
- Retirement Age
- Product You Deal In
  - Garments (checkbox)
  - Home Textile (checkbox)
- Logo Upload
  - Upload PNG/JPEG.
  - Preview displayed after successful upload.
- Product Line
  - New product line name
  - Add button
  - Existing lines displayed with Delete buttons.

ACTIONS
- Save Company Profile
  - PUT `/api/company/profile` with all form values.
  - Updates company record used by other modules and sample invoice.

- Add Product Line
  - POST `/api/company/product-lines`.
  - Refreshes the list from backend.

- Delete Product Line
  - DELETE `/api/company/product-lines/{id}`.

- Upload Logo
  - On file selection, reads the image and sends base64 data to
    `/api/company/logo`.
  - On success, updates logo preview.


7.3 Warehouses – `warehousesPane`

HOW TO ACCESS
- From Business Setup tabs, select "Warehouse" or left Setup → Warehouse.

WAREHOUSE LIST
- Shows existing warehouses with:
  - Name
  - Warehouse Type
  - Address summary
  - Delete button

NEW WAREHOUSE MODAL

Fields:
- Warehouse Name
- Address Type
  - Shipping Address / Warehouse Address / Store Address / Billing Address.
- Warehouse Type
  - Retail / Wholesale / Distribution / Store / Fulfillment.
- Address 1 / Address 2
- City
- State
- Postal Code
- Country (predefined list; e.g., Bangladesh, China, India, Pakistan, etc.)

Buttons:
- Reset – clears all text fields.
- Cancel – closes modal without saving.
- Save – POST `/api/company/warehouses`.


7.4 Factory/Land – `factoryPane`

FIELDS
- Factory Address 1 / 2
- City
- State / Province
- Postal Code
- Land Area (numeric)
- Area Unit
  - Square Feet / Square Meter / Acre / Hectare.
- Ownership Type

ACTION
- Save
  - Sends the factory/land details to backend (implementation-dependent).


7.5 Spaces – `spacesPane`

PURPOSE
- Maintain list of physical spaces (rooms, halls, production areas) with
  dimensional and safety information.

CONTROLS
- Search field – filters by Name/Purpose/Type.
- Export Excel – downloads `spaces.csv` with all rows.
- Export PDF – opens a print window containing a tabular report.
- New Space – opens Space modal.

TABLE COLUMNS
- Space Name
- Purpose
- Floor
- Space Type
- Width
- Length
- Height
- Unit (Meter/Feet)
- Capacity
- Ventilation
- Exit Plan (image thumbnail)
- Actions (Edit, Delete – Edit currently placeholder).

NEW SPACE MODAL FIELDS
- Space name (required)
- Type (required)
- Purpose
- Width, Length, Height
- Unit (Meter/Feet)
- Floor
- Capacity per unit / # of equipments
- Ventilation
- # Doors
- # Windows
- Emergency Exit plan (image upload)

ACTIONS
- Save
  - Validates required fields.
  - POST `/api/company/spaces`.
  - If an exit plan image is selected, a second POST sends the base64 image to
    `/api/company/spaces/{id}/exit-plan`.

- Delete
  - DELETE `/api/company/spaces/{id}`.


7.6 Assets – `assetsPane`

PURPOSE
- Record and manage company assets (machinery, equipment, etc.).

CONTROLS
- Search – filter by asset name/type/supplier.
- Export Excel/PDF – similar to spaces.
- New Asset – opens asset modal.

TABLE COLUMNS
- Asset Name
- Qty
- Asset Type
- Purchase Date
- Purchase Price
- Supplier
- Notes
- Saved On
- Actions (Edit – placeholder; Delete).

NEW ASSET MODAL FIELDS
- Asset Name (required)
- Asset Type
- Quantity
- Purchase Date
- Purchase Price
- Supplier
- Notes

ACTIONS
- Save
  - POST `/api/company/assets`.
- Delete
  - DELETE `/api/company/assets/{id}`.


7.7 Certifications – `certsPane`

PURPOSE
- Manage certifications and compliance documents.

CONTROLS
- Search
- Export Excel/PDF
- Add New – opens certification modal.

TABLE COLUMNS
- Certificate Name
- Certificate Image
- Valid From
- Valid Till
- Certificate Logo
- Certificate Detail
- Actions (Delete)

ADD NEW CERTIFICATION MODAL FIELDS
- Type (e.g., Ethical Labor)
- Policy (e.g., Fairtrade Textile Standard)
- Name
- Certificate Valid From
- Certificate Valid Till
- Detail (if any)
- Upload Certificate (image file)
- Upload Certificate logo (image file)

ACTIONS
- Save
  - POST `/api/company/certifications` with metadata.
  - If images selected, send them as base64 data to
    `/api/company/certifications/{id}/image` and `/api/company/certifications/{id}/logo`.
- Delete
  - DELETE `/api/company/certifications/{id}`.


7.8 Unions – `unionsPane`

PURPOSE
- Track labor unions or worker committees associated with the company.

TABLE COLUMNS
- Name
- Description
- Actions (Edit, Delete)

UNION MODAL FIELDS
- Union Name (required)
- Description

ACTIONS
- Save
  - POST or PUT to `/api/company/unions`.
- Delete
  - DELETE `/api/company/unions/{id}`.


7.9 Business Agent (embedded in `profile.html`)

PURPOSE
- AI-driven assistant that reads text/files and proposes structured database
  updates for safety/business data.

FORM FIELDS
- Text area: instructions or context (optional).
- File upload: typical input is a document (e.g., scan, PDF, etc.).
- Submit button.

FLOW
1. User enters optional text and/or uploads a file.
2. On submit:
   - If file is present:
     - FormData is posted to `/api/safety/agent/upload`.
   - Else:
     - JSON payload posted to `/api/safety/agent/propose`.
3. Server responds with:
   - Proposal ID
   - Extracted facts (bulleted list)
   - Proposed changes (per table, action, payload).
4. UI shows:
   - Proposal number
   - Extracted Facts list
   - Proposed Changes list
   - Buttons: **Approve & Apply**, **Reject**.

APPROVAL/REJECTION
- Approve & Apply
  - POST `/api/safety/agent/proposals/{proposalId}/approve`.
- Reject
  - POST `/api/safety/agent/proposals/{proposalId}/reject` with a reason.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8. EMPLOYEES & ROLES MODULES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

8.1 Employees (`/employees.html`)

PURPOSE
- Manage tenant employees (user accounts, roles assignments at a basic level).

FIELDS & CONTROLS

Top row:
- Tenant ID – ID of the tenant.
- **Load** – loads employees for that tenant via `/api/tenant/{tenantId}/employees`.
- Text: link to Roles page.

Add Employee section:
- Email
- Full name
- Password (optional; can be auto-assigned server-side)
- Title
- Role name (optional; e.g., "HR Manager")
- **Add** button

Employees table:
- Name
- Email
- Title
- Owner (Yes/No)
- Roles (comma-separated string from backend)

PERMISSION AWARENESS
- The page checks current permissions via `/api/permissions`.
- If the user does not have `USER_MANAGE`, some input and buttons may be
  disabled for security.

WORKFLOW
1. Insert Tenant ID (or let system detect from /api/auth/me).
2. Click **Load** to view current employees.
3. To add an employee, fill the Add Employee form and click **Add**.
4. Check results in the table.


8.2 Roles (`/roles.html`)

PURPOSE
- Define roles with permission sets and assign them to users.

FIELDS & CONTROLS

Top row:
- Tenant ID
- **Load** – load roles for tenant.
- Link back to Employees page.

Left pane – Create role:
- Role name input (e.g., "HR Manager").
- Permissions list (checkboxes)
  - Fetched from `/api/permissions`.
  - Displays permission code and module name.
- **Create role** button
  - POST `/api/tenant/{tenantId}/roles` with roleName and permissionCodes.

Right pane – Existing roles & assignments:

- Existing roles table
  - Name
  - System (Yes/No – indicates whether role is system-defined.)

- Assign role to user
  - User ID
  - Role ID
  - **Assign**
    - POST `/api/tenant/{tenantId}/assign-role` with userId and roleId.

WORKFLOW
1. Ensure Tenant ID is set (auto-detected via `/api/auth/me` when possible).
2. Use **Load** to fetch existing roles.
3. Create new custom roles by checking permissions and clicking **Create**.
4. Assign roles to users using their User ID from the Employees page.


