9. HR & PAYROLL MODULE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

9.1 HR & Payroll Main (`/hr/index.html`)

PURPOSE
- Comprehensive HR screen for:
  - Creating and maintaining employee profiles.
  - Managing HR/Payroll totals (MTD, QTD, YTD, etc.).
  - Listing all employees.

LAYOUT
- Top header: HR & Payroll – Add New Employee.
- Icon links to other HR pages: Job Posting, Job Postings list, Search
  Applicants, Shortlisted Applicants, and shortcut to Add New Employee.
- Tabs: Add New Employee, Totals, Payroll Details.
- Bottom: Employees table.

9.1.1 Add New Employee Tab

FIELDS (represent key HR attributes; not exhaustive):

- Employee Name *
- Email Address *
- Active (checkbox)
- Address 1, Address 2
- Phone
- Country, State/Province, Zip/Area Code, Fax
- Employee Type (Salary/Commission/Hourly/Salary+Commission)
- Department (Marketing, Sales, HR, Merchandising, Accounts, etc.)
- SS Number / NID
- Hire Date
- Birthday
- Commissionable (Yes/No)
- Commission Percent
- Next of Kin Name & Number
- Source Type (Customer, Direct, Magazine, etc.)
- Industry
- Geographical Location (Urban/Rural)
- Any Disability (Yes/No)
- Work-Injury Victim (Yes/No)
- Health Insurance (Yes/No)
- ID Number
- Heritage
- Sexual Orientation
- Notes
- Job Description

ACTIONS
- Clear
  - Resets the form.

- Save
  - If `currentEmpId` is not set:
    - Validates that Name and Email are present.
    - POST `/api/hr/employees` to create a basic employee record.
    - Obtains returned employee ID.
  - PUT `/api/hr/employees/{id}` with full HR data from the form.
  - Shows success or error via alerts.


9.1.2 Totals Tab

FIELDS
- Month/Quarter/Year to Date values for:
  - Gross
  - State
  - FICA/EOBI
  - Local
  - Federal
  - Other

Each has MTD, QTD, YTD numeric inputs.

ACTIONS
- Back
  - Reloads totals from backend for currently selected employee.

- Save
  - PUT `/api/hr/employees/{id}/totals` with current numeric values.

USAGE
- Select an employee from the list below (Edit button).
- Switch to Totals tab to view and modify payroll totals for that employee.


9.1.3 Payroll Details Tab

- Currently contains placeholder text describing that Payroll Details (Salary
  Scale, Pay Frequency, etc.) will be implemented in future iterations.


9.1.4 Employees Table

COLUMNS
- Employee ID (CompanyUserId)
- Name
- Department
- Email
- Phone
- Country
- Active (Yes/No)
- Actions (Edit)

ACTIONS
- Edit
  - GET `/api/hr/employees/{id}`.
  - Populates the Add New Employee form with existing data.
  - Loads the Totals via `/api/hr/employees/{id}/totals`.
  - Scrolls to the form and selects the main tab.


9.2 Job Posting (`/hr/job-posting.html`)

PURPOSE
- Create and edit job postings.

FIELDS
- Job Title *
- Department
- Location
- Employment Type (Full-time, Part-Time, Contract)
- Salary Range
- Application Deadline (date)
- Job Description
- Required Qualification
- Desired Qualification
- Statements
