-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12. SAFETY & COMPLIANCE MODULES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

12.1 Safety Audits (`/safety-audits.html`)

PURPOSE
- Plan audits, manage audit checklists (audit sheets), capture issues,
  generate RFQs, handle supplier quotes, and track invoices.

KEY CONCEPTS
- Tenant ID (internal; currently set in script as `1`).
- Audit Plan – top-level safety audit event (name, type, company, date).
- Audit Items – rows of checklist (Head, Value, No Issue, Issue Details, etc.).
- RFQ – Request for Quotation associated with an issue.
- Quotes – supplier responses to RFQs.
- Invoices – financial documents associated with approved quotes.

LAYOUT

A. Search + Top Buttons
- Search bar (by name, type, status) – filters audits.
- **Plan New Audit** – opens Plan modal.
- **Export to Excel** – placeholder; currently just alerts.

B. Plan New Audit Modal

Fields:
- Audit Name (e.g., "Q3 Fire Safety Review").
- Audit Type / Related To (FIRE, STRUCTURAL, UNIFIED SAFETY, etc.).
- Audit Company (external auditor name).
- Audit Date.

Action:
- Save Audit
  - Validates name.
  - Calls `SafetyAPI.createAuditPlan` with tenantId, auditName, auditType,
    auditCompany, auditDate, createdBy.
  - Shown in audits list after reload.

C. Quote Dashboard

- Counters (Submitted, Approved, Delivered)
  - Loaded via `SafetyAPI.getQuoteStats({ tenantId })`.
- Filters
  - Item
  - Supplier
  - Status (All/Submitted/Approved/Delivered)
  - Min/Max Amount
  - Sort (date, amount, item alphabetical)
- Table (RFQ lines)
  - Audit Name
  - Item Name
  - Detail
  - Qty
  - Unit
  - Amount (based on quotes)
  - PO Number (if approved quote exists)
  - View Terms
  - View Quotes
  - View Invoice

D. Audits List

- Table columns:
  - Audit Date
  - Audit Name
  - Related To (Type)
  - Status (NEW, PENDING CORRECTION, CLOSED)
  - Action (View)
  - Certificate (View, if Closed)

- View
  - Loads detailed plan and items via `SafetyAPI.getAuditDetails(Id)`.
  - Opens detail card below with safety audit sheet and issues view.

E. Safety Audit Sheet (Detail Card)

- Header shows audit title, company, date, and plan status.
- Audit sheet table columns:
  - HEAD
  - VALUE
  - NO ISSUE (checkbox)
  - ISSUE DETAIL (textarea)
  - ATTACHMENT (file upload, stored as base64 string)
  - SUGGESTED ACTION (textarea)
  - INFORMED TO (text)

Usage:
- Each row corresponds to an audit item.
- By default, rows with no issue details are considered "No Issue".
- Uncheck "No Issue" and fill Issue Detail, Suggested Action, Informed To,
  and attach proof if there is a finding.

Save Audit Sheet:
- **Save Audit Sheet** button collects all rows and calls
  `SafetyAPI.saveAuditItems(auditId, items)`.
- On success, shows success message and reloads audits list.

F. Open Issues & Corrective Actions

- Displays a card per item that has an issue (No Issue == false or IssueDetails
  not empty).

Fields per issue card:
- Read-only summary (Head, Value, Issue details, Suggested Action, Informed To).
- Corrective Action section:
  - Corrective Action Taken (textarea)
  - Attachments (URLs)
  - Corrective Action By
  - Corrective Action On (date)
  - **Save Corrective Action** – calls
    `SafetyAPI.submitCorrectiveAction(auditId, itemId, payload)`.

G. RFQ Section for Each Issue

- Button: **+ Create RFQ** – toggles RFQ form.

RFQ Form Fields:
- Item Name
- Qty
- Unit (select; options retrieved from `SafetyAPI.listUnits()`;
  can also add a new unit inline).
- Needed By (date)
- Detail (free text, often pre-filled with issue/ action summary).
- Recipients (emails, comma separated)
- Shipping Terms
- Payment Terms
- Other Terms

Action:
- **Send RFQ** – calls `SafetyAPI.createRFQ(data)`.

RFQ List
- Below form a text list shows all RFQs for this issue via
  `SafetyAPI.listRFQByItem(itemId)`.

H. Quotes Overlay

Access:
- From Quote Dashboard table, click **Quotes** button.

Overlay content:
- Meta line: RFQ ID, item name, qty, unit.
- Quotes table columns:
  - Supplier
  - Price
  - Shipping
  - Tax
  - Discount
  - Total
  - Arrival date
  - Status
  - Actions: Approve (with PO number), Mark Delivered, Invoice.

Actions:
- Approve
  - Takes PO number input and calls `SafetyAPI.approveQuote(id, po)`.
- Mark Delivered
  - `SafetyAPI.updateQuoteStatus(id, 'Delivered')`.
- Invoice
  - If invoice exists: show invoice number & total.
  - Else: prompt user and call `SafetyAPI.createInvoice(quoteId, data)`.

I. View Invoice (from Quote Dashboard)
- If an approved quote has an invoice, shows invoice number and total.
- If not, allows creating one using prompts.


12.2 Safety Training (`/training.html`)

PURPOSE
- Maintain a log of safety training sessions, with attendees and export.

FIELDS
- Name
- Related To
- Date
- Conducted By
- Description
- Attendees (multi-select list of employees loaded from
  `/api/tenant/1/employees`).

ACTIONS
- Save Training
  - Calls `SafetyAPI.createTrainingSession(payload)`.

- Reset
  - Clears form and resets current session ID.

- Search + Download CSV
  - Search filter (Name/Related To).
  - **Download CSV** – exports visible table rows.

LIST TABLE
- Columns: Date, Name, Related To, Conducted By, Attendees (#), Actions.

Actions:
- Edit – loads selected session and attendees back into form.
- Delete – removes session via `SafetyAPI.deleteTrainingSession(id)`.


12.3 Other Safety‑related Pages

- `test-fire-form.html`, `audit-verification.html`, `auditor-audit-sheet.html`
  implement specialized forms for particular audit or verification workflows.
  They follow the same pattern: labeled fields, save/submit buttons,
  tables displaying previously saved rows.


