13. TASKS & CALENDAR MODULES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

13.1 Task Management Hub (`/tasks/index.html`)

PURPOSE
- Explain Task Planning concept and link to planner stub.

CONTENT
- Title: Task Management.
- Description of planned React TS implementation (MiniCalendar, timeline,
  TaskFormModal).
- Card linking to Task Planner:
  - **Open Planner** → `/tasks/planning.html`.


13.2 Task Planner / Calendar (`/calendar.html` and `/tasks/planning.html`)

PURPOSE
- Visual calendar with a 24‑hour timeline for assigned tasks per employee.

LAYOUT

Left card (Month selector):
- Prev / Next buttons
- Month label (e.g., "January 2026")
- Month grid (7 columns: Mon–Sun) with day cells:
  - Today is highlighted.
  - Selected date is highlighted.
  - Muted days for previous/next month.
- Instruction: click a day then click a user/time slot.

Right card (Timeline):
- Header row
  - First column blank, followed by 24 columns for hours 0:00–23:00.
- For each employee (row):
  - First cell: employee name.
  - 24 hourly slots.
  - Tasks appear as colored "pills" spanning one or more hour slots.

TASK CREATION MODAL
- Opened by clicking an empty slot.

Fields:
- Start (datetime-local)
- End (datetime-local)
- Task (title; required)
- Priority (High/Medium/Low)
- Description
- Upload Image
- Assign To (employee dropdown, from `/api/tenant/{tid}/employees`)
- Assign By (read-only current user name from `/api/auth/me`)
- Repeat
  - Does Not Repeat / Daily / Weekly / Monthly / Annually
  - When a repeat is chosen:
    - Sub-options appear (e.g., every N days for Daily).
    - End mode: indefinitely / until date / repeat N times.

Actions:
- Back – closes modal without saving.
- OK – saves task.

SAVE LOGIC
- Prepares payload with:
  - date (selected day),
  - startHour / endHour (derived from times),
  - title, description, priority, assigneeId,
  - encoded repeat information appended to notes.
- Sends data to `/api/tasks` via helper.
- Closes modal and refreshes timeline.


